The iris transition leaks a 256 x 256 texture on every level load (the memory growth)

Every level load runs Transition_Init, which calls g_holeFX.Init. Init first asks D3DApp::CreateTextureSurface for a
viewport-sized capture surface (the "frozen frame" iris). CreateTextureSurface only creates one when the pointer it is
given is still null, and HoleFX never releases its capture surface: so the first load creates it, and on every later
load CreateTextureSurface returns E_FAIL. Init then takes its other branch (the circle-mask iris) and makes a new
256 x 256 ARGB4444 Texture, overwriting maskTexture without deleting the previous one. From the third load on, each load
leaves one texture behind: 128 KB of pixels (a managed or system-memory surface, so in the game's own memory) plus the
Texture object, which is the "a little more memory with every load" seen in Task Manager.

This fix keeps the existing mask texture and redraws it instead of making a new one. It does not change which iris is
used: the first transition after start-up still uses the frozen-frame iris and every later one the circle mask, as in
the original.

Touches: src/fx/holefx.cpp (HoleFX::Init).

diff --git a/src/fx/holefx.cpp b/src/fx/holefx.cpp
index fc01b6a..89d22a3 100644
--- a/src/fx/holefx.cpp
+++ b/src/fx/holefx.cpp
@@ -235,7 +235,12 @@ void HoleFX::Init(D3DApp *app, void *viewport, float radius, u8 useCubicBezier)
     if (this->app->CreateTextureSurface(&captureSurface, (s32)this->viewport->viewportWidth,
                                         (s32)this->viewport->viewportHeight) < 0) {
         hasCaptureSurface = HOLEFX_MASK;
-        maskTexture = new Texture(this->app, 0x100, 0x100, TEXFMT_ARGB4444, &result);
+        /* FIX iris-mask-leak: Transition_Init calls Init on every level load. The capture surface of the first load is
+         * never released, so CreateTextureSurface fails on every later one and Init comes here each time; the
+         * original made a new 256 x 256 mask texture here and overwrote the previous one without deleting it (128 KB
+         * of pixels per load, from the third load on). The existing mask is kept and redrawn instead. */
+        if (maskTexture == 0)
+            maskTexture = new Texture(this->app, 0x100, 0x100, TEXFMT_ARGB4444, &result);
         BuildCircleMask();
         screenRadius = sqrt(this->viewport->viewportWidth * this->viewport->viewportWidth / 4.0 +
                             this->viewport->viewportHeight * this->viewport->viewportHeight / 4.0);
